  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 34e3dacc4599bc547af4a43b0b848c66, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Note: "Important steps: \n0. Add an EyeOutlet (from the EDIA_LSL package) to this
    GameObject.\n1. Add, if not there, the [EYE] DataHandler prefab to the scene.\n2.
    Add this GameObject to the list of dataclients (it's important that the \"EyeDataClientLslPusher\"
    is the upper most component on the GameObject!).\n3. Make sure that both \"EyeDataClientLslPusher\"
    and \"EyeOutlet\" use the same Eye\n4. Set the Sampling Rate on the \"Eye Outlet\"
    to the SR of your Eye Tracker (e.g., 120 Hz for the Vive Pro Eye) if the tracking
    is implemented accordingly; otherwise set it to the display refresh rate (e.g.,
    90 Hz)"
